{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851822-world-of-darkness-comics-and-mangas","id":851822,"title":"World of Darkness Comics and Mangas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-23T09:26:39-07:00","id":851822,"title":"World of Darkness Comics and Mangas","content":"And now for something, Completely Different.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes yes yes, we always talk about movies and books...but what about comics to influence the World of Darkness? to get us ideas and such?.<br /> and also..WHAT DOES IT TAKES TO RELAUNCH THE WORLD OF DARKNESS COMICS?!.<br /> <br /> So, heres some personal recommendations<br /> Hellboy and BPRD. Not only a great story, but interesting inspiration for technocracy/son of Aether games.<br /> The Crow: Goes with out saying.<br /> Gotham Central: the comic that inspired Gotham Police Department.<br /> Johnny The Homicidal Maniac: i think this one embodies perfectly what a Marauder Is.<br /> Fables: If you need inspiration for changeling, then grab Fables.<br /> <br /> theres a few i hear by name but i havent explore yet, like American Vampire or Saga (i been told its pretty much Changeling the dreaming)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:53:18-07:00","id":851992,"title":"","content":"mmm...I can't think of anything great:<br /> <br /> Murcielago (Manga): if you don't know how Dementation works.<br /> <br /> Sex Criminals (Comic): for Changelings...I use it for Sabbat games, though.<br /> <br /> Ghost in the Shell (Manga): I'm not a big fan. But I use it for Pentex/Techno/Sabbat games set in 21-22nd century (Along with Deus Ex).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Johnny The Homicidal Maniac: i think this one embodies perfectly what a Marauder Is. </div> </div> </div>never heard of that one, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 03-23-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:39:57-07:00","id":853149,"title":"","content":"More Recomendations<br /> <br /> Preacher. Just Preacher by Garth Ennis.<br /> <br /> Hellblazer: a must read for any Mage the Ascension player<br /> <br /> The Mask: The comic that inspired a very loosely adaptation. Perfect for Freak Legion<br /> <br /> American Vampire : havent read this one, but i been told is Sabbat the comic<br /> <br /> 30 Days by Night/Dark Days/Return to Barlow: Sabbat/Hunter<br /> <br /> 100 Bullets: Euthanathos<br /> <br /> Men in Black by Malibu Comics: The comic that inspired the Movie..More dark and little bit more gritty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Manga<br /> <br /> Fuan No Tane: A bunch of Short stories set on modern japan. using both elements inspired by local urban legends and other mythologies, interesting for getting ideas to explore<br /> <br /> Uzumaki: The mystery of the Spirals, perfect for anything Wyrm related.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 03-25-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:43:32-07:00","id":853198,"title":"","content":"Spawn by Todd MacFarlane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:41:53-07:00","id":853596,"title":"","content":"Neil Gaiman's Sandman: want a hundred cosmologies and myths all together in one place? great for changeling, mage, werewolf and wraith<br /> <br /> Books of Magic: almost essential reading for Mage<br /> <br /> Lucifer: did some one say Demon: The Fallen?<br /> <br /> Justice League Dark is a bit more superheroy but can be some good fodder for more action oriented games<br /> <br /> Annihilation, Annihilation Conquest, War of Kings, Realm of Kings and the Thanos Imperative is great for a Void Engineers game or any game set out in the deep umbra<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T00:36:27-07:00","id":854907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851822-world-of-darkness-comics-and-mangas#post851822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and also..WHAT DOES IT TAKES TO RELAUNCH THE WORLD OF DARKNESS COMICS?!.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how well the Vampire books from Moonstone fared, but as a W:tA fan: The Werewolf ones weren't that great. I think the only one that was good was the Get of Fenris one, otherwise a lot of them ran on the same beats (<i>Like the 'time to shoehorn in a well-known character for no reason' beat</i>) or were waaay too short to cover the stories they wanted to tell.<br /> If they were to relaunch them, it would be better to follow just one Garou pack and how they develop over the series, rather than various different characters that we don't get to know very well all the time.<br /> <br /> <b>My list:</b><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride_of_Baghdad\" target=\"_blank\">Pride of Baghdad by Brian K. Vaughan and Niko Henrichon</a> (<i>A small pride of Simba</i>)<br /> First Moon by Jason McNamara and Tony Talbert (<i>Deals with Roanoke and the Croatoan</i>)<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Moon\" target=\"_blank\">High Moon by Gallaher and Ellis</a> (<i>World of Darkness in the Wild West</i>)<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strangeways_%28comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">Strangeways: Murder Moon by Matt Maxwell and Luis Garagna</a> (<i>Werewolf: the Wild West</i>)<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginga_Legend_Weed\" target=\"_blank\">Ginga Legend Weed by Yoshihiro Takahashi</a> (<i>W:tA. Period.</i>) <br /> <br /> <b>As for my goofy/classic 90's choice:</b><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mighty_Mutanimals\" target=\"_blank\">Mighty Mutanimals from Archie Comics</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:03:26-07:00","id":854912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851822-world-of-darkness-comics-and-mangas?p=854907#post854907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginga_Legend_Weed\" target=\"_blank\">Ginga Legend Weed by Yoshihiro Takahashi</a> (<i>W:tA. Period.</i>)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As fan of the series, what in it makes you feel it fits WtA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:44:55-07:00","id":860560,"title":"","content":"The Invisibles - another great read for Mage. The enemy is a great inspiration for both the Technocracy and the Nephandi (they're more Seers from Awakening than Technocracy, but their control over the world is still similar, as is the idea that they've shaped the consensus of reality in their own image). The magic isn't explained fully at any point, and each character has their own flavor, being very similar to how magic has its own flavors and paradigms for each mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:31:42-07:00","id":863192,"title":"","content":"Sandman by Neil Gaiman : For changeling<br /> The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen: For technocracy<br /> The Crow: Personally, ill go for the Eric Draven story (The one that inspired the movie) and Curare<br /> American Gothic: The Swamp Thing by Alan Moore<br /> From Hell by Alan Moore: A must read for any mage the ascension Dm who wants to explore the method to Madness of Jack the Ripper, his Ascension and slow turn into a Marauder.<br /> Tales from the Crypt: The quintessencial horror comic book from E.C comics. even if the stories might come pretty tame for now standards, its a must read.<br /> The Chilling Adventures from Sabrina : A more mature and horror take on the story of Sabrina the Teenage Witch. Pretty interesting stuff for anyone into Mage<br /> Neonomicon: By Alan Moore, a modern retake on the Cthulhu Mythos. WARNING: Might get a bit rapey<br /> <br /> Shade the Changing Man: Another vertigo title, where madness is the weapon and also the cause <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> very interesting takes for a marauder protagonist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"ht